          {
            "command": "taskfleet run salvage",
            "about": "Salvage a stuck single-worker run: fence its prior worker (verifying identity first) and drive `run merge` from the preserved worktree's current git state — the fenced manual finish for an `attention-required` run (a worker that exited cleanly but skipped `run merge`) or a `failed` run whose branch was preserved. Refuses an already-`done`/`cancelled` run, a multi-node run, a run with no preserved worktree/branch, and a live worker it cannot safely fence",
            "aliases": [],
            "hidden": false,
            "deprecated": false,
